DESIGN GOAL:

I wanted each soldier to have a role in the battle that would improve their teamwork. My main focus was making the footman and archer stick together to complement their strengths. 
I believe that the archer was the most valuable piece, so I focused on giving it a playstyle that kept it alive. I put less focus on the knight because I wanted it to be an annoyance that diverted attention from the knight
and archer.

REFLECTION:

In my code, I used distance calculations to get the distance between enemies and allies so that my units would make moves based on those distances. At first, I struggled with how to do that as I was trying to directly
get their distances from the dictionaries but I instead switched to individual calculations by using help from the coding agent.

AI USE:

I used the GitHub Copilot coding agent. When I got stuck trying to get the distances of allies and enemies and make my units move accordingly, I had it help me design code to get my desired results.
It also helped with modifying their behavior when certain things happened in the game, like when an enemy got too close or when it saw a specific ally. I checked the result by watching the AI play, playing the
game against my AI to see how it responded to specific scenarios, and by double-checking any generated code.
